===== Installation =====

<WRAP center round important 100%>
Some newer devices use an XM25QH64C flash memory chip that was not supported in OpenWrt until ''22.03.4''. Installing earlier OpenWrt releases will brick those devices. Unless you really know what flash chip you have, you should install ''22.03.4'' and later.
</WRAP>

<WRAP center round important 100%>
**Devices running these early OEM firmware versions MUST first be upgraded to a later OEM version before attempting to install OpenWRT**, as the older flash partition layouts are incompatible with these images and you could risk bricking your device.

  * 3.0.0 Build 20200314 Rel.3608
  * 3.0.0 Build 20200508 Rel.41814

All later releases use the same consistent flash layout documented below and are safe to use ([[commit>?p=project/firmware-utils.git;a=commit;h=8a8da19aea57cef6ad0e73355023304aebf7c467|Ref]]).
</WRAP>

<WRAP center round important 100%>
**OpenWrt versions ''23.05.4'', ''23.05.5'' are known to brick these units** ([[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/bricked-tp-link-tl-wpa8631p-v3/151594/76|thread]], [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/tp-link-wpa8631p-v4-bricked-trying-to-install-23-05-4-release/210914|thread]]) and will require opening up the unit and using Serial uboot + TFTP recovery. **Until the issue is resolved, you should only install version ''23.05.3'' and lower**.
</WRAP>

